From fbe0df9ab0bc1e88fa20866b6e8f9aaf1740b017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:50:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] VPVulkan: timestamp queries from the GPU frame times
 (occlusion: visible)

New src/queries.cpp. Queries written by a command buffer are stamped at vkQueueSubmit with the
core frame that executes them. A TOP_OF_PIPE timestamp reads as that frame's GPU start, any later
stage as its end, in host-clock nanoseconds (timestampPeriod 1); results are available once the
frame completed (WAIT, WITH_AVAILABILITY, PARTIAL, 32/64-bit honoured). gpu/metal2 reports
GPUStartTime/GPUEndTime per command buffer through GpuTimings, and vpgpu::Device keeps the last
512 for lookups (frameTimes). This gives Source 2's adaptive fidelity real GPU frame times
instead of zeros. Per-pass timings (Metal counter samples at encoder boundaries) are not wired to
queries. Occlusion queries report 1 (visible). vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults writes what is
available when recorded.

Test: gpu_vulkan.sync (timestamps not ready before the frame completes, then start/end).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P8F98JbsaD2Vbgvi6v4LyY
